---
description: Server-side remote handler rules for Roblox
globs: "src/server/**/*.luau"
alwaysApply: false
---

Every `OnServerEvent` / `OnServerInvoke` handler must:

1. Treat its arguments as untrusted. Check `typeof` for each one and bounds for numbers (reject NaN: `x ~= x`).
2. Check permission and game state on the server (ownership, cost, distance, cooldown).
3. Rate-limit per player.
4. Compute outcomes on the server. Never accept amounts, damage, prices or positions as facts.

```luau
--!strict
local Remotes = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage"):WaitForChild("Remotes")
local Shop = require(script.Parent.Shop)

local lastCall: { [Player]: number } = {}

Remotes.BuyItem.OnServerEvent:Connect(function(player: Player, itemId: unknown)
	if typeof(itemId) ~= "string" or #itemId > 64 then return end
	local now = os.clock()
	if (lastCall[player] or 0) + 0.5 > now then return end
	lastCall[player] = now
	Shop.tryPurchase(player, itemId) -- looks up the price server-side and checks the balance
end)

game:GetService("Players").PlayerRemoving:Connect(function(player) lastCall[player] = nil end)
```

Never use `InvokeClient`. Never `loadstring` anything.
